{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>Swarming winged creature</b> — These are the small, low-creeping creatures that swarm upon the earth, such as flies, hornets, mosquitoes, and locusts. This is the language of Rashi (Rashi on Leviticus 11:20). But this is not correct in my view, for a bird would not be called a שֶׁרֶץ on account of its smallness, nor would its name be simply \"bird\" (עוֹף) on account of its body's size. The bat has small legs, and many species of locust have legs larger than its — so why should it not be called שֶׁרֶץ הָעוֹף like them? Rather, שֶׁרֶץ הָעוֹף means in its adjacent phrase \"that goes on four\" — for every bird that walks on two legs has an upright neck and its head raised upward, and it relies on its wings and flies continually; therefore it is called עוֹף כָּנָף and simply עוֹף. But creatures with four legs walk low, with their neck and head downward like swarming creatures, and therefore they are called שֶׁרֶץ הָעוֹף, as I explained in the book of Genesis (Genesis 1:20). And so He returned here and explained: \"Every swarming winged creature that has four legs is an abomination to you.\" Its meaning is as if saying: every swarming winged creature that has only four legs and does not have the jointed legs mentioned — it is an abomination to you. And its midrash in Torat Kohanim (chapter 5, section 10): Rabbi says: \"And every swarming winged creature that has four legs\" — this implies that if it has five, it is pure. Now in this section there is regarding שֶׁרֶץ הָעוֹף only a positive commandment, but in the repetition of the Torah (Deuteronomy 14:19) a prohibition is stated concerning it: \"And every swarming winged creature is impure to you; it shall not be eaten.\" From there one receives lashes for it."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {0 "Ramban's parenthetical biblical references are embedded in his Hebrew text; I have rendered them as he wrote them, including his citation of Torat Kohanim by chapter and section number."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:52:54.146486384Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}